{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Compact articulation field for REAPER MIDI Editor. Requires js_ReaScriptAPI and ReaImGui, installed separately through ReaPack. Supports per-track banks, keyswitches, MIDI channels and controllers. Personal banks are stored outside this package and are not distributed. Licensed under MIT; see LICENSE.md and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ArticulationBox\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 By {\b Andrey Novikov}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b English} \u183 ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "README_RU.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
\u1056 ?\u1091 ?\u1089 ?\u1089 ?\u1082 ?\u1080 ?\u1081 ?
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 User guide: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ArticulationBox/USER_GUIDE.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
English
}}}
 \u183 ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ArticulationBox/USER_GUIDE_RU.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
\u1056 ?\u1091 ?\u1089 ?\u1089 ?\u1082 ?\u1080 ?\u1081 ?
}}}
. Open {\b Help} in the full script menu for offline explanations.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A compact articulation menu for the REAPER MIDI Editor.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 One ReaPack package includes the embedded articulation field, a quick menu at the mouse cursor, and a full settings menu. It supports manual and automatic keyswitches, MIDI channel switching, independent track banks, default articulations, keyswitches that follow musical notes, and keyswitch pitch protection during transposition. The script interface is in English.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install with ReaPack\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Import this repository URL:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/andreynovikov86-cmd/ArticulationBox/main/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 In REAPER, open {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Import repositories} and paste the URL. Then open {\b Browse packages}, find {\b ArticulationBox}, choose {\b Install}, and click {\b Apply}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The script requires {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/juliansader/ReaExtensions"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
js_ReaScriptAPI
}}}
 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reaimgui"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaImGui
}}}
 for the parameter editor. Install both separately through ReaPack and restart REAPER after installing the extensions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 First run\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Open a MIDI item. In {\b Actions > MIDI Editor}, run {\f1 Articulation_Manager.lua}. Assign a shortcut to {\f1 Articulation_Quick_Menu.lua} in the same action section for quick articulation selection. Keep the main script running so it can update linked keyswitches.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Create a bank through {\b Settings > Banks > New} and add entries through {\b Add / Edit articulation}. Enable {\b Settings > Run script on startup} for automatic startup. Save your project to restore track bank choices and note assignments.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Personal banks, projects, and user backups are not included in this repository. When moving from a manual installation to ReaPack, reassign your shortcuts to the actions from the new installation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 For a full installation guide in Russian, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ArticulationBox/INSTALL_RU.txt"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
INSTALL_RU
}}}
. Third-party code acknowledgments are in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ArticulationBox/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Articulation editor\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Add / Edit articulation uses one compact, resizable window with {\b Keyswitch}, {\b Channel}, {\b KS + Channel}, and {\b Controller} choices. Play a MIDI key or click a piano-roll key to fill the keyswitch note and velocity, then edit either value if needed. {\b Save & Next} builds several mappings without reopening the editor. Window size is remembered. The Bank line identifies the destination; the Articulation list selects a new or saved mapping, and Remove articulation deletes a saved mapping. Full-menu choices live under Articulations; same-pitch velocity variants have their own submenus. The shortcut still opens choices directly.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Choose {\b Before note start} or {\b After note start} and set Delay in milliseconds. A delayed keyswitch can trigger a loop ending after a chord starts, with independent keyswitch velocity. Automatic keyswitches still follow the musical note\u8217's end.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Manual keyswitches\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 You can draw and edit MIDI notes directly on articulation rows. These notes do not receive a default articulation. Their latest switch remains active until the next explicit automatic assignment on the same MIDI channel.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 If you independently change an automatic keyswitch's pitch, position, length, or velocity, it becomes manual. Its previous automatic assignments are removed while the musical notes are preserved. Moving musical notes still moves their linked automatic keyswitches.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 When a later keyswitch starts on the same MIDI channel, the earlier keyswitch is shortened to end at that point. Musical note lengths are preserved.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Updates\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 To install updates, use {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Synchronize packages}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 To publish a new release, change the package code, increase {\f1 @version} in {\f1 ArticulationBox/Articulation_Manager.lua}, update {\f1 @changelog}, and push to {\f1 main}. The workflow uses the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
official ReaPack indexer
}}}
. Existing indexed versions are retained, and download links refer to fixed commits.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 License\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ArticulationBox is licensed under the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "LICENSE.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
MIT License
}}}
, which permits use, modification and redistribution, including commercial use, with the required copyright and license notices.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Adapted Gridbox code retains its original MIT copyright and license notice in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ArticulationBox/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
}}}
. Both notices are included in the ReaPack package.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Controllers\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Save Pitch Bend or any CC as an independent named preset, or attach it to an articulation. Ready menus show {\b Controller} when presets are available or assigned controllers can be reset. {\b Reset controllers} clears controllers from selected notes while preserving articulations. Choose {\b Full note}, {\b Note start}, or {\b Note end}, with Before/After margins and a reset value. Pitch Bend, Mod Wheel and Hold Pedal appear first in the chooser. Controllers follow note edits and Undo/Redo; see the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ArticulationBox/USER_GUIDE.md#controllers"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
user guide
}}}
.\par}
}
